^2}$; in the matter era the potentials of a growing perturbation do not change with time.","caption":["The plane of $\\eta$ and $x$ through the centre of the well ($y = z = 0$), which light launched along $x$ never leaves, since the well is symmetric about it. Its rays are null geodesics with $dx/d\\eta = \\pm\\sqrt{(1 + 2\\Phi)/(1 - 2\\Psi)}$, from which the scale factor drops out.","The cones are narrowest at the centre of the well, where light crosses $0.82\\,L$ of $x$ in each $L$ of $\\eta$, and they open toward $45°$ outside it. A ray that crosses from $x = -1.5\\,L$ to $1.5\\,L$ takes $0.37\\,L$ more conformal time than it would with no well. The Kretschmann scalar diverges at $\\eta = 0$, the big bang of the dust."],"source":{"fields":["coords","parameters","metric_components","inverse_metric_components","kretschmann","domains"],"version":"37e0dfccd1a17528"},"slices":[{"view":"well","surface":0,"label":"$\\eta = L$","version":"b0b2b8d61f0c291a","lines":[[[0.0,0.3333],[1.0,0.3333]]],"points":[],"fills":[],"place":{"at":[1.0,0.3333],"anchor":"br","dx":0,"dy":-1.3}}]}],"longitudinal_curved":[{"id":"well","label":"through the well","plane":["\\eta","x"],"families":["moving left","moving right"],"xlabel":"$x/L$","ylabel":"$\\eta/L$","ticks":{"x":[{"at":-1.5,"label":"$-1.5$"},{"at":-1.0,"label":"$-1$"},{"at":-0.5,"label":"$-0.5$"},{"at":0.0,"label":"$0$"},{"at":0.5,"label":"$0.5$"},{"at":1.0,"label":"$1$"},{"at":1.5,"label":"$1.5$"}],"y":[{"at":0.0,"label":"$0$"},{"at":0.5,"label":"$0.5$"},{"at":1.0,"label":"$1$"},{"at":1.5,"label":"$1.5$"},{"at":2.0,"label":"$2$"},{"at":2.5,"label":"$2.5$"},{"at":3.0,"label":"$3$"}]},"box":[-1.5,1.5,0,3],"to_display":[[0.0,1.0],[1.0,0.0]],"mirror":false,"rays":{"P":[[[0.0572,-0.0211],[-0.0206,0.0495]],[[0.1233,-0.0216],[0.0528,0.0457],[-0.0214,0.1128]],[[0.1877,-0.0204],[0.1384,0.0293],[0.0864,0.0798],[0.0334,0.1293],[-0.0205,0.1778]],[[0.2537,-0.021],[0.1885,0.0481],[0.1215,0.1154],[0.0509,0.1826],[-0.0214,0.248]],[[0.3198,-0.021